# Phase 7: model kinds (render::models). An ngspice `r` or `c` model, a
# level-3 diode and the R/C cards naming them are written for Spectre and
# VACASK through one row per ngspice parameter; a D card's parameters are
# Spectre's (`pj` is `perim`, names lowercased: Spectre is case-sensitive);
# a resistance reading v(), i() or temper is written as ngspice runs it (a
# noiseless B source keeping tc1, tc2, m) on Spectre, and on VACASK when it
# reads only temper (`$temp`), else refused there. A bare `parser` in an
# ngspice `.options` (Xyce's option package) is not written, a repeated
# option keeps its last value, and VACASK takes `scale`. The
# baseline is baseline-daa0ad0-fx13: fx11 with the four T-M decks
# (tests/spectre/t_m*.scs) added to its manifest, which have no output there.
fixtures/tests/spectre/t_m1_resistors.scs cdl a new input: tests/spectre's T-M deck for a real Spectre (tests/test_model_kinds.rs), in baseline-daa0ad0-fx12's manifest with no output
fixtures/tests/spectre/t_m1_resistors.scs espice a new input: tests/spectre's T-M deck for a real Spectre (tests/test_model_kinds.rs), in baseline-daa0ad0-fx12's manifest with no output
